      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Pillars of Alra [zone=812]\n**Who:**\n- Il`Nendale of Erion [npc=38839]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 81\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Faction Required:**\nPurity of Alra (between Dubious and Ally)\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Purity of Alra +?\n**Factions Lowered:**\n- Shades of Alra -?\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Fal`Kaa`s Shadowward [npc=39077]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Pillars #1: The First Pilgrimage [quest=5481]\n- Pillars #2a: The Word of Melretia [quest=5482]\n- Pillars #2b: The Word of Anriella [quest=5483]\n- Pillars #2c: The Word of Fal`Kaa [quest=5484]\n- Pillars #3: Crisis of Faith [quest=5486]\n- The Growing Threat [quest=5493]\n- The Truth [quest=5492]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Nov 29 23:29:39 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This shared task (1-6 players) begins with Il`Nendale of Erion in the Pillars of Alra, located outside the northwestern pillar 630, 330, 515._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"The First Pilgrimage\"\n\\- 81 Skill Level in Alaran\n\\- Minimum \"dubious\" faction with \"Purity of Alra\"\n\\- Less than maximum 'ally\" faction with \"Purity of Alra\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Il`Nendale of Erion'\nIl`Nendale of Erion says, in Alaran, 'A plague upon the heads of the corrupted! There is only one path and it is through light! The [false teachings] of stoicism and indifference that our mortal enemies preact shall be their undoing!'\nYou say, 'False teachings?'\nIl`Nendale of Erion says, in Alaran, 'I have no doubt you already know of the basic falsities being purported by the dark ones?' It continues without waiting for you to answer, 'We must put an end to this! Only the true [wishes of Alra] shall be known throughout the world!'\nYou say, 'What wishes of Alra?'\nIl`Nendale of Erion says, in Alaran, 'As we have already discussed, the final wishes of Alra were many but absolute. Deviation from the great one's truth is grounds for execution. I shall speak of the truth if you will [assist] in our crusade against the corrupted ones!'\nYou say, 'I'll assist you'\n_If you have max ally faction with \"Purity of Alra\", you see this, and get attacked afterwards:_\nIl'Nendale of Erion shakes its head from side to side, 'The purity of Alra shall someday touch your people as it has ours. Until that day that you bring word of conversion, or the news of our enemey's destruction, we have nothing to speak about. Begone.'\n_If you have less than max ally faction with \"Purity of Alra\", it goes on as normal:_\nIl`Nendale of Erion says, in Alaran, 'Very well, do away with a number of the deceptive xeretics ko that our world will be one step closer to purity and harmony!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Word of Erion'.\nThe creatures surrounding the tower act as conduits for the power of shade. Cleansing these creatures will make it more difficult for the Agents of the Black to expand their power beyond their walls.\nThe lower caste that survey and toil in the lower halls of the pillar are responsible for sustaining the dark mana pool. Shining a light of purity on these dark halls will weaken the heretics significantly.\nThe foyer is sparsely occupied. Residents of this hall will make it a point to hide in the shadows like cowards.\nWithin the dark meditation halls are a number of souls unable to escape the enthralling allure of darkness. Free them from their agony.\nThe Agents of the Black are ruthless in their extraction and corruption of power. Destroy the shaded ones before they are able to amass any more mana.\nPerhaps the most dangerous of the Pillar's inhabitants are the spreaders of false truth. Silencing these charlatans is the most important duty you could perform for the Pillar of Light.\nIl`Nendale does not believe you to be within your power to eliminate the personal guard of Fal`Kaa...\n\n---\n\n_NOTE: While you have this task, you will have an effect called \"Agents of Light\" on you, making you kill-on-sight to mobs inside the Pillar of the Black._\nShine a light upon the dark creatures around the pillar 0/3 (Pillars of Alra)\nEnter the depths of the pillar and eliminate some of the lower caste 0/4 (Pillars of Alra)\nPurify the barren foyer of its heretical inhabitants 0/3 (Pillars of Alra)\nAwaken some of the audience from their corrupted meditation 0/2 (Pillars of Alra)\nDisrupt the dark ritualists in the shadow infusion halls 0/3 (Pillars of Alra)\nCleanse the library of its malevolent practitioners 0/4 (Pillars of Alra)\n_These are straight kill updates. You need to kill mobs in the different levels of the Pillar of the Black._\n(Optional) Strike at the heart of Fal`Kaa and eliminate two of its Shadowwards 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Mobs called \"Fal`Kaa's Shadowward\" are found on the very top floor of the pillar. These mobs are more difficult than your standard Pillars of Alra population. They hit for a max ~16,000._\nReport your success to Il`Nendale 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ With your honorable duties completed, return to Il`Nendale and report your success.\nYou say, 'Hail, Il`Nendale of Erion'\nIl`Nendale of Erion begins flipping through the pages of a small tome and reciting a bit of its dogma, 'The Way of Light, Alra's Last Wishes, VIII of IX... When the final days are upon us we will be ready to enact the Plan of Finality, to rely on ourselves as the chosen keepers of Alra's wishes...'\nYour faction standing with Purity of Alra got better.\nYour faction standing with Shades of Alra got worse.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nElatarki's Diary - Four Cornered\n- Eltarki's Diary - Four Cornered [item=100418]\n- Fragment of Legendary Alaran History [item=100964]",
    },
