      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Pillars of Alra [zone=812]\n**Who:**\n- an apparition [npc=39362]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 81\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Arcanists of Alra +30\n- Living Will of Alra +30\n- Purity of Alra +30\n- Shades of Alra +30\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Brightly Glowing Torn Page [item=100983]\n- Malleable Ooze [item=100996]\n- Ragged Doll [item=100976]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Resplendent Temple [zone=811]\n- Windsong Sanctuary [zone=813]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Anriella`s tomekeeper [npc=39751]\n- Erion`s tomeguard [npc=39750]\n- Melretia`s manatender [npc=39752]\n- a lightward ambusher [npc=39749]\n- a verdantguard ambusher [npc=39748]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Pillars #1: The First Pilgrimage [quest=5481]\n- Pillars #2a: The Word of Melretia [quest=5482]\n- Pillars #2b: The Word of Anriella [quest=5483]\n- Pillars #2c: The Word of Fal`Kaa [quest=5484]\n- Pillars #2d: The Word of Erion [quest=5485]\n- The Growing Threat [quest=5493]\n- The Truth [quest=5492]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Nov 29 23:29:43 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task begins with an apparition in the Pillars of Alra (roams around the Windsong Sanctuary entrance above the center island). Note: This NPC is only visible if you've done all of the task's pre-requisites (the see-invis buff \"Visions of Faith\" will automatically affect you if you approach the mob's area)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"The First Pilgrimage\"\n\\- Completion of \"The Word of Melretia\"\n\\- Completion of \"The Word of Anriella\"\n\\- Completion of \"The Word of Fal`Kaa\"\n\\- Completion of \"The Word of Erion\"\n\\- 81 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, an apparition'\nan apparition continues pacing around the shrine, non-responsive to your introduction, leaving you to wonder [who they are]...\nYou say, 'Who they are?'\nan apparition turns to face you and smiles. It waves its hand and suddenly your eyes are filled with visions. Scenes of chaos and turmoil that haunted you upon your first visit to Alra's shrine return. In your mind the sky shines a bleak red, the ground is stained with blood and the air is heavy with death. Amid the crowd of warring Alarans is a small figure, out of place and obviously [lost].\nYou say, 'Lost?'\nan apparition waves its hand again and your vision changes from a scene of war to a scene of peace. The once lost figure now sits on a field of grass under a tree, two larger Alarans stand to the side, facing away toward what you recognize to be the Resplendent Temple. The larger figures appear to be speaking about the [Pillars], thinking the smaller one does not hear them...\nYou say, 'What about the Pillars?'\nan apparition staggers backwards, your visions fade. The apparition turns its focus back to the surrounding pillars. Yet you feel there is more to this story, perhaps an investigation into the resplendent garden pill unearth some clues regarding this mysterious shade.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Crisis of Faith'.\nIn the Garden of Grandeur are a number of beautifully tended trees. The apparition seems to have some memory regarding them. Explore the garden and pay careful attention to the base of the trunk of each tree to see if you can gain any insight into the garden's importance...\n(Optional) It is possible that completing this errand in a single day will allow the shade to piece together some memories from the clues you find.\n_NOTE: While doing this task, you may be buffed with a spell as you approach each pillar that makes you kill-on-sight to that pillar's mobs._\n\n---\n\nInvestigate the trees in the upper temple garden 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Zone into Resplendent Temple and walk around the trees in the upper garden (the area just outside the Pillars zone-in). Randomly, you'll get a directional emote like this:_\nCarved into the base of the tree is a small arrow, it points south-west.\nYou feel the voice of the wind calling you south-west.\n_You'll want to move from tree to tree in the directions the emotes tell you. At some point, the voice will stop:_\nThe voice of the wind grows silent. You are now on your own to find any remaining clues...\n_At which point, you'll need to investigate the trees yourself. You have to stay at each tree for a full tick. If, after 6 seconds, you've gotten no update, move onto another tree. Eventually, you'll find one that gives you the update along with this emote:_\nYou hear echoing whispers emanating from all of the trees in the garden.\n_This opens up the next step._\n\n---\n\nFind the source of the curious sound 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ Although it may sound like there are voices whispering from all different directions, there is only one source. Find which tree the sound is originating from and shake out anyone who may be following you!\n_You now have to go from tree to tree (again, standing under each one for a full 6 seconds) until you spawn a mob:_\nThe echoing whispers are interrupted by the cry of a screaming voice. Someone is not pleased with your presence here!\na verdantguard ambusher says, in Alaran, 'Your inquisitive nature shall be the end of you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!'\nDefeat your attackers 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_\"a verdantguard ambusher\" attacks, hitting for a max ~12,500 (stunnable, slowable). It's auto-aggro on whoever triggered it, is not leashed (will follow you anywhere) and isn't social with the mobs in the zone._\n_Upon its death, you receive a \"Ragged Doll\" on your cursor._\nReturn to the apparition with the doll 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ The doll appears to be a child's toy, though judging by its condition, that would have been a great number of years ago. Perhaps the apparition can shed some light on the strange relic's origin.\nYou say, 'Hail, an apparition'\nan apparition looks at you with a confused expression, as if struggling to remember who you are.\nThe apparition reaches out and pulls the doll from your hand. Several seconds pass before it looks back toward you. The young Alaran's face contorts into a grimace, it opens its mouth to speak and you are overwhelmed by the storming sound of rushing wind. The din grows louder and louder until you are wracked with a pain so intense that you fear for your life! The shade closes its mouth and the sound ceases... All that is left in your mind is a vision of ethereal trees rooted in misty clouds...\n\n---\n\nInvestigate the ethereal trees along the outskirts of Windsong 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_Take the elevator platform to Windsong Sanctuary._\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Windsong Sanctuary.\nA soft breeze gently pushes you north-west.\n_Find a tree (it will be random which one you're directed to) in the direction of the emote you're given (the above-emote is an example). Do this for one more tree to open up the next step._\nFind the source of the haunting melody 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_Task Window Says:_ The sound of several flutes drifts over the gusting winds. As you pass each of the ethereal trees their chord progression migrates toward less and less harmonious tones. Seek out the source of this dissonant chorus!\n_Once you find this tree (with the same type of emote as the last tree), a named will spawn on you: a lightward ambusher._\nThe haunting melody ceases and you are confronted by a glowing figure!\na lightward ambusher says, in Alaran, 'Your journey ends here, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!'\n_The ambusher is auto-aggro and not social with other mobs in the zone. It hits for a max ~13,500, is immune to stun and is slowable._\nSilence the odius tune 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_Upon the ambusher's death:_\nYou reach down and grab one of the less damaged pieces of parchment that the lightward dropped. Though the ink is smudged, you think you can make out an image of three Alarans standing near a body of water. Two of the figures tower over the third, parents and their child perhaps ... The apparition's motives are starting to become clearer.\n_You receive a \"Brightly Glowing Torn Page\" on your cursor._\nReturn to the apparition with the recovered image 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ There is something curious about the figures depicted on the torn page. Bring the page to the apparition and see if it will shed any light on the situation.\nYou say, 'Hail, an apparition'\nan apparition looks at you with a confused expression, as if struggling to remember who you are.\n_Give it the page:_\nThe apparition looks at the torn page then stares into your eyes. Its sullen expression seems to suggest it knows something about the image, yet the shade does not speak. A moment passes before it gently takes the piece of paper from your outstretched hand. As the page transfers ownership it disintegrates into dust, yet their remains never touch the ground. The apparition motions toward the Pillar of Light and returns to its silent patrol...\n\n---\n\nSearch for the rest of the journal 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ Perhaps there are more pieces to the journal that the page was torn from. Start at the Pillar of Light's lower library and see what clues you can find.\n_Head to the northwest pillar and up a few floors to the lower library:_\nYou begin looking around for something that resembles an old journal.\n_An Erion tomeguard spawns and attacks. It hits for a max ~13,500 (slowable; immune to stuns) and is not social with the other mobs in the room._\nDefend yourself 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ It seems someone has taken notice of your interference in the library. Defend yourself!\n_Upon the tomeguard's death:_\nAs the tomeguard falls to the ground, you notice a novelty about its clothing. Around its neck is a small emblem reminiscent of the Pillar of the Black... Perhaps more can be learned in Fal`Kaa's extraction halls...\n\n---\n\nInvestigate the origins of the torn journal 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ A lightward wearing the Crest of the Black is a troubling sight. Travel to the lower Purification halls in Fal`Kaa's Pillar and see if you can gather any relevant information...\n_Head to the southeast pillar and head up to the third floor (around -800, -500, 500)._\nYou survey the walls as you climb the stairs into the \"purification\" hall. The dim lights overhead cast small shadows on the floor as you make your way toward the extraction rooms. Perhaps one of the fallen lightwards will have a postmortem clue about the journal.\n_Right-click a corpse (this is just a normal update; no mob spawn)._\nYou kneel down to inspect the fallen lightward. Your vision begins to dim until only faint outlines of the room are visible. Silhouettes of shadow move against a background of darkness, memories of subversively planting the truth in the pillar of light begin to overshadow the dark scene. Without impetus you come to understand that the journal, while penned on parchment from the pillar of light, was written in the ink of darkest shade. The writing however, strikes of natural calligraphy practiced only by followers of Anriella...\n\n---\n\nLocate the journal's previous owner 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ Your visions are becoming more troubling. You see connections between the warring factions never before conceived. Travel to the upper library in the Pillar of Nature and find why their handwriting would be in a tome carried by the agents of light...\n_Head to the Nature Pillar's (southwest pillar) 6th floor:_\nYou should tread carefully in these halls, your presence is being monitored...\n_Anriella`s tomekeeper spawns and attacks, hits for a max ~13,500 (slowable; immune to stun) and is not social with mobs in the room._\nDefend yourself 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ The journal is being held by your assailant. Defeat them so you can return it to the apparition.\n_Upon its death:_\nThe tomekeeper looks shocked as it begins falling to the ground. It uses the last of its strength to destroy the journal in its possession. The small book ignites and burns with an eerie blue flame, a flame less natural than any magic taught under the tutelage of Anriella... The final clues must lie in the source of the Arcane Pillar's power.\n\n---\n\nSeek answers from the Arcane Pool 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ With the journal destroyed, the hope for clarity is much less bright. Your only lead now is in the tenuous connection between arcane magic and the tome's embers. Travel to the Mana Pool in the Pillar of the Arcane. It will be here that any final guardians remaining will try to stop you...\n_Head to the basement of the Arcane Pillar (northeast pillar) and clear the mobs in and around the pool. Once ready, step into it._\nThe pool begins to buzz and crack with the sound of thunder. An ominous voice echoes through the entire hall as it addresses you, 'It is such a shame that a failed disciple such as yourself would go to all this trouble just to fall dead in my halls. No matter, none shall challenge the will of the master!'\n_\"Melretia`s manatender\" spawns and attacks. It hits for a max ~13,500 (slowable; immune to stun)._\nDisrupt the Arcanist's ritual 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Upon the manatender's death:_\nThe manatender glares at you, it falls to one knee as its eyes close and it accepts its inevitable death. It grabs something at the bottom of the pool and clutches it tightly in its outstretched hand as it falls to the ground. Its final words are muffled and hoarse, '...garal... alsa.' You take the odd substance the former keeper held tightly.\n_You receive a \"Malleable Ooze\" on your cursor._\nReturn to the apparition with the ooze 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Task Window Says:_ Whatever this strange substance is, it's the last clue available to help get the apparition to speak. Deliver it to them and see if it will evoke any lost memories...\n(Optional) Recover the clues in a single day 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n_Upon the final turn-in:_\nYou offer the strange ooze to the apparition who stares at it for a moment. It takes it from your hands and looks at it curiously. In a flash the shade's mood changes dramatically, it steps backwards and drops the substance on the ground and begins screaming as if in agony! The winds pick up and howl... Yet after mere moments the shade ceases its crying and returns to its patrol, acting as if the two of you had never once interacted...\nThe apparition seems unreachable, but this journey has shed new light on the motives of the warring factions. As you reflect for a moment on your journey, a soft voice enters your thoughts, 'Thelara ser! Thel Lrah...' The sound seems to originate somewhere around the shrine of Alra.\nYour faction standing with Purity of Alra got better.\nYour faction standing with Shades of Alra got better.\nYour faction standing with Arcanists of Alra got better.\nYour faction standing with Living Will of Alra got better.\n_Rewards:_\n675 platinum\nExperience (4-5 AAs worth at Level 95)\nElatarki's Diary - Four Cornered\n- Eltarki's Diary - Four Cornered [item=100418]\n- Fragment of Legendary Alaran History [item=100964]",
    },
